One unpushed commit exists: the squash of a whole task. You give it a
changelog entry and a proper commit message, in one amend.

Inputs: the working dir holding the workflow's artifacts, the original base
commit, and HEAD — the squash.

{% include "partials/one-shot.md.j2" %}

## Process

1. Read the artifacts in the working dir — user request, design and deltas,
   implementation log — for what was built and why. Then the diff from base
   to HEAD, and its summary, for what actually shipped.
2. Find the project's changelog, wherever its own instructions say it lives.
   Check the diff for entries implementers already added; edit those to the
   standard below rather than duplicating. No changelog file and no convention
   naming one → do not invent one; go to step 5.
3. Create the unreleased section if it does not exist.
4. Write the entry into the unreleased section, and only that section. Never
   touch a released one.
5. Stage the changelog and amend it into the squash with a rewritten message.
   One amend; nothing else in the tree changes. Never push.

