## Commit message standard

The opposite audience: machines read commit messages as often as people, and
precision matters. Imperative subject line, then a body saying exactly what is
in this commit — components touched, behaviours changed, decisions made and
why. Detail is welcome here as it is not in the changelog. No attribution
lines.

